 talkie of T5 is bought, held out (the radio on for him on every machine, the model in his hand on the host's screen) and put away again by a CLIENT, and a CLIENT takes hold of a guard's body, the host moves it along his path while the client's own screen shows it follow, and he lets go; it found a real bug, now fixed: a body dragged by a client was let go at once on the host, because `DraggableBody` asked the dragger's `isActiveAndEnabled` and the `WobblyPlayer` of a player on another machine is switched off on every machine but his own (`NetPlayer.OnNetworkSpawn`), so it now asks whether his object is in the scene). NOT checked: with the real keys and by hand; a body dragged through a closed sliding door; a busted teammate over the network (only the guards' bodies are in `DragNet`).
